{
    "background_story": "Stanley was a master typesetter in the early days of printing. He spent most of his career working with metal type, carefully arranging individual characters to create beautiful typography. Stanley's specialty was kerning, the delicate art of adjusting the space between letters to create a harmonious flow. He took great pride in his work, often spending hours perfecting the kerning on a single page. His attention to detail and passion for typography earned him a reputation as one of the finest typesetters in the city. When the digital age arrived, Stanley was hesitant to adapt, but he eventually found a new appreciation for the precision and control offered by computer-aided design. He continued to work on typography projects, always mindful of the importance of kerning in creating visually stunning text.",
